  "implementation": "The global control stores independent zero-C K16 WMMA values and absolute dots in one bounded 16-query slab; a separate kernel applies the original ordered K32 alphas and one explicitly rounded FP32 addition per K16. The shared candidate exchanges four K16 groups in 8192 bytes of LDS and reduces them in the same order within one kernel. Both transports must preserve identical raw proxy and bound bits. The original 2^-19 error coefficient, deferred finalization, reciprocal and BF16 endpoint predicate remain. The approximate FP32 carrier changes relative to original carried WMMA, so independent native envelope tests and complete GB10 boundaries are required; raw equality with the original approximate carrier is not presumed.",
